From ee8d9693748d627a4843703bb734bb913e7736af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 17:01:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Module plans: HexaTech Loyalty and Content on their own, 85
 EUR each

The owner (2026-11-02): customers buy one product at a lower price and add
the others later. The loyalty application (hotel-tech-loyalty,
App\Support\PlanModules) gives an organisation whose plan holds only these
products the matching workspaces, and adds a product by moving the
subscription to the plan of the larger set through change-plan (Stripe
prorates the one price).

- Migration: product `content`; plans `loyalty` (8500), `content` (8500)
  and `loyalty-content` (17000), EUR, monthly only, 7-day trial, their
  products and features. Created hidden and without Stripe prices, so
  nobody signs up for or moves to one before it can be charged.
- stripe:sync --plan=<slug>... --publish: price only the named plans,
  then make each public once it has its monthly price.
- SubscriptionService::changePlan refuses to move a Stripe-charged
  subscription to a plan with no price for the interval (before, the
  local plan changed while Stripe kept charging the old price).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
